			<div class="content" id="post-content-1993869">
									

<p>I like the skip, but the interview doesn't seem to add much. It's just a neighbour who's got no information to give - beyond their own mild puzzlement that some would care for spiders.</p>
<p>The bit about the spiders living in interdimensional space didn't really go anywhere. Why can't they just live inside the old woman's body - helping aged internal organs to keep working, or replacing them entirely.</p>
<p>The latter would be a bit like one idea in David Cronenberg's film Shivers (aka They Came from Within). A parasite that takes over the function of a faulty organ.</p>
<p>Overall, it's like a benign version of the plot of Phase IV.</p>

